  "notes": "US/ANSI (layout id 0x01). Control interface 2, transaction id 0x1F (0x3F also answers), extended matrix 5×15 with column 0 unused, backlight LED 0x05. Verified on firmware 1.12: firmware/serial/layout read, effect + brightness read. LED matrix matches OpenRGB's Huntsman Mini keymap. Fn layer: Fn+1…= → F1–F12 is confirmed by Razer; Fn+Backspace → Delete and Fn+I/J/K/L → arrows come from reviews, and other legends (media, volume, brightness, gaming mode, macro, sleep) could not be verified from the master guide (its keycap diagram is an image only), so they are left out. Wave direction bytes (0/1) follow OpenRazer's daemon table and are not verified. Interface 3 is a Windows Dynamic Lighting LampArray; KeyHalo drives the keyboard natively and skips it."
